<ol>
<li class="css-1ksqbpg">
<p><strong>PARSE_SYNTAX_ERROR at <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">ROUND</code></strong> — The aggregation expressions (<code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">ROUND(...)</code>, <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">COUNT(...)</code>, <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">MIN(...)</code>, <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">MAX(...)</code>) were floating as standalone fragments without a <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">SELECT</code> keyword, commas between columns, or a proper <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">FROM</code> clause. I assembled them into a single valid <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">SELECT ... FROM ...</code> statement. The <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">MIN(Revenue)</code>/<code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">MAX(Revenue)</code> references to the column alias <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">Revenue</code> were also invalid (aliases can't be used in the same <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">SELECT</code> level), so I replaced them with the full expression. The final <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">SELECT product_category product_type</code> was missing a comma and <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">FROM</code> clause — now fixed.</p>
</li>
<li class="css-1ksqbpg">
<p><strong>CAST_INVALID_INPUT</strong> — The <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">REPLACE(unit_price,','',''.')</code> had malformed quote placement, so it wasn't actually converting commas to periods. Fixed to <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">REPLACE(unit_price, ',', '.')</code> across all 3 occurrences. This correctly transforms European-format prices like <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">"3,1"</code> → <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">"3.1"</code> before casting to DOUBLE.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Results confirmed:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li class="css-1ksqbpg">Aggregation: 149,116 products sold, $698,812.33 total revenue, 9 distinct categories, per-transaction revenue range $0.80–$360.00</li>
<li class="css-1ksqbpg">Product query: returns category/type pairs successfully</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Heads-up on two other issues I noticed but did not touch</strong> (per your "fix only the focused cell" instruction):</p>
<ul>
<li class="css-1ksqbpg"><code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">USE CATALOG brightcoffeeshop.sales.coffee_shop</code> — <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">USE CATALOG</code> expects only a catalog name, not a 3-part table reference. This will error when running all statements.</li>
<li class="css-1ksqbpg"><code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">DAYNAME()</code> in Databricks returns full names like <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">'Sunday'</code>, but the <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">CASE</code> checks for short forms like <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">'Sat'</code>, <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">'Sun'</code> — so <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">Day_of_the_week</code> will return <code style="color: rgb(232, 236, 240); font-size: 0.85em; line-height: 20px; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; background: rgb(55, 68, 79); font-family: monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 4px; border: unset; margin: 0px;">NULL</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Would you like me to fix those as well?</p>
